#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# around

#% text
# `around(x, dx)` represents the value `x` with the standard uncertainty `dx`.

#% text
# `around(list)` gives the mean of the list with its standard deviation as the uncertainty.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Arithmetic and functions propagate the uncertainty to first order, assuming independent arguments: f(x +- d) is f(x) +- |f'(x)| d.

#% item
# The centre and the uncertainty are machine numbers.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
around(1/2, 0.01)
#% output
#= around(0.5, 0.01)

#% cell
around(1.0, 0.1) + around(2.0, 0.2)
#% output
#= around(3.0, 0.223606797749979)

#% cell
sin(around(1.0, 0.1))
#% output
#= around(0.8414709848078965, 0.05403023058681398)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
gamma(around(2.5, 0.01))
#% output
#= around(1.329340388179137, 0.009347345216260855)

#% cell
around(2.0, 0.1)^2
#% output
#= around(4.0, 0.4)

#% cell
around([1.1, 0.9, 1.0, 1.2])
#% output
#= around(1.05, 0.12909944487358055)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `interval`, `centered_interval`, `mean`, `std_dev`
